      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T17:50:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good call. I poked into this\n\n1.  Yes there\u0027s a bunch of pRPC calls to LUCI services that dont require credentials (confirmed with a cleared LUCI_CONTEXT and isolated empty HOME)\n2. Cuz of that, the proactive \u0027bb auth-info\u0027 i added to the start of bb_wrapper scripts didnt make sense. I dropped it.\n3. Now we check bb auth-info on failures and append the suggestion for auth-login if it makes sense.\n\nAlso.. on why `bb auth-login` in the first place?   While both bb and the prpc binary share the same token store... bb auth-login is the most userfriendly.  luci-auth login requires manually passing the exect scopes string. \n\nAnyway. I think were we ended up is great. Low-friction but helpful in the case of failure. Mostly :)   \n\nappreciate this!",
